WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Literature Club

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.770
Hiya, President!

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:08.690
Hey, you guys!

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.670
What happened to your head?!

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.460
Oh, this?

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.500
I got my fortune told by this psychic
everyone's been raving about lately.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.830
She told me I can improve my luck
by wearing ultra-flashy hairstyles.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.830
Did... it actually work?

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:24.750
Sure did!

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.750
As soon as I left the house,
a total hottie came up and talked to me!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.000
Excuse me, ma'am.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.880
May I see some identification?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.630
He thought you were suspicious!

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.500
Gentle words

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.630
Soft feelings

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:48.540
Precious memories

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.070
They're dyed with love

00:00:55.130 --> 00:01:01.330
When I'm with you, even getting caught
in the rain turns into something new

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.580
What words can I string together

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.710
To keep this color from fading away?

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.290
I know

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:15.210
What the two of us will 
become on that far-off day

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.630
Isn't that right, God?

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.130
Waiting for the train, the 
water droplets beading up

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.710
I really wish this moment

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.710
Could somehow last forever

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.750
Is that too much to ask?

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:42.000
Poem 5:    The Fortune Teller Girl
Fortunes

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.830
Wow, that's really cool!

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.060
I love things like horoscopes

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.210
And fortune telling!

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.380
Even you can't resist girly 
stuff like that, huh?

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.330
So the psychic I mentioned...
She only sets up shop on Sundays.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.040
I'd like to see her!

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.530
President, please let me know

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.580
Where I can find her!

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.720
You bet! I'll message you the address.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.980
You're not into fortune telling, Eiji-kun?

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.170
Nah, I just don't get the hype!

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.860
The whole idea of "predictin' the future"
seems way too convenient.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:17.630
It's all, "Who were you in a past life?" and
"What do your palm lines say about you?"

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:21.120
Then they got "soul numbers" 
and "conjunctions"...

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.630
"The twenty-seven lunar mansions" this
and "numerology" that...

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.920
You know a lot for someone
who supposedly hates this stuff.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.750
What's wrong?

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.960
President...

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.580
I respect you as my upperclassman,
so I'm gonna say this as delicately as possible...

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.250
I...

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.920
I've never seen anyone look
as dumb as you do right now!

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.350
That wasn't delicate at all!

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.850
Oh, is that it over there?

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.070
Had a feelin' there'd be a line...

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.850
Huh?! Big Sis Koto?!

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.920
Oh my! On a date, are we?

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:11.170
I'm guessin' you came 
to see the psychic, too?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.960
That's right! I've got unique palm lines,
so I wanted to have them read.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:16.960
Huh...

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.830
See for yourself!

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.920
Doesn't my life line seem unusually long?

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.890
5:00
Lotion
Every Hole

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.890
I'm way more concerned about
the note written on your hand!

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.930
Nanako-chan, about this...

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.290
Wh-what the hell did you 
say to her, Big Sis Koto?!

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.710
Next guest, please.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.000
Go ahead and take my place 
in line. See you later!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.330
Now then, what would you like to know?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.010
I want to know how

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.280
Compatible I am with

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.460
My friend over there!

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.510
J-just as friends, nothing else.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.000
Understood. I shall determine 
your compatibility.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:08.750
God... Just this once and
then I'm never doin' this crap again!

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.370
Thank you so, so much!

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.730
Ei-chan, you really are a

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:13.690
Super nice person!

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.500
Gah... C'mon, cut it out!

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.790
You're gonna embarrass me!

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.280
Embarrassed or not,

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.600
I still appreciate it.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.900
So thank you, Ei-chan!

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.360
O-okay... read our fortunes, 
but make it quick!

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.170
First, I'll need your names.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.780
Of course! My name is

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.120
Nanako Yukishiro.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.170
It's nice to meet you!

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:34.040
Last name: Busujima! First name: Eiji!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.040
Pleasure to meetcha.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:39.340
Nanako Yukishiro-san and Eiji Busujima-san...

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.920
Ooh, I see...

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.260
How very interesting...

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.040
This is...

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.750
I've never seen anything like it.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.570
Wh-what's it say?

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.060
To be frank, you're utterly incompatible.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.670
I've never seen two people as
ill-suited for one another as you.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.460
What?! A-are you serious?!

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.130
It's really that bad?!

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.000
You go together worse than
an unpopular celebrity and internet trolls.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:19.080
I-I don't think that's true at all...

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:27.880
NOTE: Tao incorrectly writes Eiji's last name using the kanji for "busu"
that translates to a derogatory word for an ugly woman.
Eiji Busujima
Nanako Yukishiro

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:27.880
Allow me to give you a more in-depth explanation.
Please take a look at this.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:28.220
NOTE: Tao incorrectly writes Eiji's last name using the kanji for "busu"
that translates to a derogatory word for an ugly woman.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.210
NOTE: Eiji's last name is actually written using the kanji for "busu"
that means "harm" or "poison."

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.210
Y-you completely screwed 
up the kanji for my name!

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.790
My apologies. Should I have used
the other version of "shima"?

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.600
NOTE: There are two different versions of the kanji for "shima"
(which change to "jima" when combined with "busu").
Tao assumes she used the wrong one.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:34.600
That's not the problem!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.170
BUSU
JIMA

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.460
Wow... I didn't realize you 
could read that as "Busujima."

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.830
Color me shocked.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.070
I think I should be the one sayin' that...

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.130
Using the incorrect name results
in an inaccurate reading.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.110
Shall I try once more?

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:52.750
I'll incorporate tarot cards this time to give you
a more comprehensive reading.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:55.170
N-no, that's not necessary.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.500
'Scuse us!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.670
Let's go, Nanako.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.000
Are you sure?

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.030
It's totally fine!

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.290
I'm pretty happy with how

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.460
This turned out, myself!

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.410
What you said back there...

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.690
He denied it right away.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:10.870
That's all I wanted!

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:13.420
To be frank, you're utterly incompatible.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:16.290
I've never seen two people as
ill-suited for one another as you.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.980
That's impossible!

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.940
It wouldn't hurt to look...

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.450
Ooh, yes, I see...

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.920
Too bad they didn't want another reading.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.330
Should we get goin'?

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.510
I-it's you, from before!

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:44.750
Oh, hello.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.500
You go to our school?!

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.290
Yes. I'm Tao Hanakai.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.630
Oh, please keep my identity a secret, okay?

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.770
"Secret"? All anyone's 
gotta do is look at you!

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.360
Not true. During the week, I disguise myself by
switching up the way I part my hair.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.230
That doesn't disguise anything.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.700
Sorry... I stand corrected.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.580
So, where are you two headed?

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:14.460
Oh, we're goin' over to Spot's 
Cho to get a work out.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:18.290
Huh... A boy taking a girl 
to Spot's Cho? I'm jealou-

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.420
Oh, I mean... That sounds 
like a terrible time.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.540
She got even scarier after 
she corrected herself!

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:28.240
Since you're here, allow me
to read your fortunes for today.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:33.740
Today is a favorable day 
for you, Yukishiro-san.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.850
You will have good luck in all that you do.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.960
As for Busujima-san...

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.060
I believe it would be in your best interest
to avoid going out today.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:48.980
I predict that lightning will
come crashing down upon you.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:52.150
Huh?! R-really?!

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.620
Um, hey, Ei-chan? I...

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.360
I'm getting kind of worried...

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.640
You feeling okay?

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.860
C'mon, Nanako. Are you still
thinkin' about what she said?

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:15.290
Don't worry! I don't believe 
in all that mumbo jumbo.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.430
Besides, blood type A is s'posed
to have the best luck today!

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:19.890
Apparently you DO believe in it...

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.820
Um, this might be weird,

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.110
But I don't actually know

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.420
How to play billiards...

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.950
Oh, for real? It's easy!

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.850
To sum it up with a senryu...

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.900
There's balls and a pole...

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.280
Thrust the pole towards the balls,

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.580
And aim for the holes

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.540
S-sorry! That sounded bad!

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:44.960
There's balls and a pole...

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.370
H-hey Ei-chan, maybe

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:47.110
Try wording that first sentence

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:48.290
A bit differently!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.990
Pardon me. May I see your ID?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.720
Huh? Oh, of course!

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:04.520
Oh come on, it's not that big a deal!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.920
This is a piece of cak-

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:11.130
I'm gonna die! I'm gonna die! I'm gonna die!

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.330
C'mere, Nanako! Grab onto me!

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.710
From the looks of it,
I got Yukishiro-san's fortune right... so far.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:32.290
What should we do next?

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.830
What about that thing you 
mentioned the other day?

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.830
I feel so lame coming here by myself...

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.260
But I want to know whether 
or not I was right...

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:40.890
Oh! Miss Psychic?

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:45.390
Thanks to you, I've had eight hot guys
come up and talk to me today alone!

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:47.350
Who are you?

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:48.330
Huh?

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:50.960
O-oh...

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.900
We go to the same school, don't we?

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.350
Yes. Oh, that reminds me, Senpai...

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.280
Is this how you write your name?

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.290
Amane Katagiri

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:02.930
No, I don't use that kanji for my first name.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.420
I'm sorry, but please stop wearing
your hair like that immediately.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:09.130
Man, that was a blast!

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.710
I haven't sweat that much in a while!

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:17.670
Plus, the weather's cleared up
and there's no sign of lightning.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:27.000
H-hey! Y-you can't just 
start stripping here...!

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.110
No need to worry!

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:37.580
I made sure that I wore a

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:38.780
T-shirt underneath!

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.750
G-gotcha... Don't give me 
a heart attack like that!

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:44.710
Oh God...

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:49.460
I had no idea Nanako's chest was that big...!

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.000
Nanako... Would you mind 
puttin' that back on for now?

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.250
Well, in a way... I guess 
my prediction came true.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:15.540
It's almost funny how different we are

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:20.920
Down to our reflections in the shop window

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:26.580
When you smile as brightly as the sun

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:35.130
A peaceful feeling washes over me

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:42.330
Even my trivial, everyday life

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:47.920
Begins to shine when I'm with you

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:51.380
Even if something happened

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:54.540
Even if we hurt each other sometimes

00:11:54.540 --> 00:12:01.880
Believe in our ordinary days

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:06.870
On the next epi-

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.240
-sode of Senryu Girl:

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.480
Nanako's Rebel-

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.780
-lious Phase!

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.960
Next Time, Poem 6
"Nanako's Rebellious Phase"
